            ("h2", "The decision that set the direction: inventory valuation"),
            ("p", "The widely reported technical root is unglamorous. Lidl valued inventory at <strong>purchase price</strong>. SAP's retail standard is built around <strong>retail price</strong> valuation. Two defensible accounting conventions, incompatible defaults."),
            ("p", "Lidl had a real reason to keep its convention: purchase-price logic was woven into how the company negotiated, priced and measured itself, and leadership was unwilling to give up something it treated as a competitive edge. So the decision was made to adapt the software to the process instead of the process to the software."),
            ("p", "Read in isolation, that is a reasonable business call. The problem is what it implies structurally:"),
